<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Rentokil on &quot;bear&quot; list.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Rentokil on &quot;bear&quot; list.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Business services group Rentokil Plc was added to the UK strategy &quot;bear&quot; or sell list at Merrill Lynch, a research note from the investment bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Industrial conglomerate BTR Plc was added to the Merrill &quot;bull&quot; list and Laura Ashley Plc was removed from the &quot;bear&quot; list.</p>
<p>Merrill strategists said Rentokil was trading on a high price-earnings (PE) multiple but concerns were mounting about its prospects, while there was less downside in Ashley shares after recent declines.</p>
<p>BTR was favoured because it has seen persistant director share buying and was on a 20 percent discount to the rest of the market in terms of its prospecting PE rating, Merrill said.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
